### 3.5 System-level energy model

For the photonic chiplet input interface at 30–108 GB/s:

| Component | Electrical (UCIe) | Optical (photonic) |
|-----------|-------------------|-------------------|
| 30 GB/s @ 0.25 pJ/bit | 7.5 W | — |
| 30 GB/s @ 5 pJ/bit | — | 150 W |
| 108 GB/s @ 0.25 pJ/bit | 27 W | — |
| 108 GB/s @ 5 pJ/bit | — | 540 W |
| 108 GB/s @ 1 pJ/bit (best research, system) | — | 108 W |
| 108 GB/s @ 0.013 pJ/bit (modulator only) | — | 1.4 W (unrealistic system-level) |

**The range is enormous: from 1.4 W (unrealistic) to 540 W (unacceptable).** The realistic system-level estimate is likely 50–150 W for the input interface alone, which may exceed the power budget of the entire electronic GPU.

