## 4. Task Deliverables

### Deliverable 1: Crossover analysis

Produce a plot or table showing:

- X-axis: bandwidth (10–200 GB/s)
- Y-axis: energy per bit (pJ/bit)
- Two curves: electrical (UCIe) vs optical (photonic), each with best-case, typical, and worst-case
- **Identify the crossover point** — the bandwidth/distance at which optical becomes more efficient

### Deliverable 2: Verification of the 30–108 GB/s range

Confirm or refute:
- That the input data volumes (Section 5 of the parent document) are correctly estimated
- Whether 30 GB/s is realistic as a lower bound (minimal G-buffer + motion vectors)
- Whether 108 GB/s is realistic as an upper bound (G-buffer + motion + neural features)
- What the actual range would be for a real workload (e.g., UE5 Nanite path tracing at 4K)

