## 5. Interface Contract (Logical Level)

This is the abstract specification the analysis should evaluate against:

INPUT SIDE (Electronic → Photonic) ────────────────────────────────── Data: G-buffer (RGBA 16-bit float) + motion vectors (2x float16) + neural features (float16 tensor) Rate: 30–108 GB/s Format: Serialized, packetized (protocol TBD — not HDMI/DP) Distance: 5–50 mm (on-package to inter-package)

OUTPUT SIDE (Photonic → Optical Display) ──────────────────────────────────────── Data: Optical image representation I(x, y, λ, t) Rate: 2–6 Gspots/s (4K@240 Hz, depending on RGB scheme) Format: Optical (no digital serialization) Distance: 10 cm – 2 m (chip to display)
The analysis should determine which side(s) should use optical interconnect, and under what conditions.

